WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.857
Here greet receives one argument.

00:00:02.857 --> 00:00:09.277
The string Avery is assigned temporarily to the parameter name while the function runs.

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:13.238
The f-string then inserts that value into the message.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.272
Change Avery to another fictional name or label.

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:22.787
The function body does not need to change because the parameter makes the function flexible.

00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:26.076
That is one of the main reasons functions are reusable.
